5,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'A gate flags a test that subprocess-execs a shell script containing an unguarded destructive deletion ... Verified by `python scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py`.'","Testing: 'flags the unguarded shape' is the RED-fixture that actually exercises the flag path","AC2/AC3 correctly cite the fixture test as their verifier; AC1 does not"],"finding":"AC1's named proving command (`python scripts/check_destructive_test_exec.py` run against the repo) proves the tree is clean, not that the gate FLAGS an unguarded destructive-deletion test. The flagging behavior is actually proven by the pytest fixture ('flags the unguarded shape') in the Testing section, not by the bare gate invocation named in AC1.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f696dfc77183f5a7b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1","norm_id":"n5562259b48654649","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor wires the gate, runs it on a clean tree, sees exit 0, and marks AC1 done without ever proving the flag-path fires against an unguarded fixture."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Change AC1's verifier to the pytest fixture that asserts the gate reports a finding on an unguarded-shape fixture, mirroring how AC2/AC3 cite the fixture test.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Address `scripts/check_shellcheck.py` / ShellCheck SC2115 as prior art: state explicitly what the new gate catches that SC2115 does not (e.g. `rm -rf \"$var\"/*` embedded as an inline script string inside a Python test file, which the existing `.sh`-only ShellCheck walk never sees), and scope the new gate to that gap rather than re-detecting standalone `.sh` files SC2115 already flags.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC: 'A gate flags a test that subprocess-execs a shell script containing an unguarded destructive deletion (rm -rf against an interpolated variable)' and 'passes a script whose deletion is guarded by `: \"${dir:?}\"` plus an explicit deny-list'.","scripts/check_shellcheck.py docstring: 'The motivating defect is SC2115:: rm -rf \"${dir}\"/*  # warning: Use \"${var:?}\" ... [SC2115] ... expanded to rm -rf /* ... destroyed /opt/homebrew and /Applications' — same incident, same shape.","check_shellcheck.py is already wired into make lint (Makefile:266) and runs SC2115 at -S warning over all scripts/**/*.sh (SEVERITY='warning' is called load-bearing precisely so SC2115 is not silenced).","Plan cites check_raw_git_writes.py and check_wall_clock_asserts.py as prior art for the GATE SHAPE but omits check_shellcheck.py, the prior art for the DETECTION TARGET.","Plausible novelty (catching rm -rf inside inline heredoc/script strings embedded in Python test files, which ShellCheck's .sh-file walk cannot see) is never stated in the plan."],"finding":"The plan proposes a new static gate whose detection target (`rm -rf` against an interpolated variable; pass `: \"${dir:?}\"`-guarded scripts) is already covered by the existing `scripts/check_shellcheck.py` gate via ShellCheck SC2115, which is wired into `make lint` and was created from the same 2026-08-26 incident — yet the plan never mentions this prior art or justifies the new tool against it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa33f503aefef10d9","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Summary + Acceptance Criteria (all four detection ACs); Notes","norm_id":"n03f6f56b423dee65","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer asks why a second bespoke AST/regex gate is needed when SC2115 already flags `rm -rf \"$var\"/*` and recommends `${var:?}`.","The new gate and SC2115 double-report on the same .sh file, or diverge on the guarded shape, producing confusing/contradictory lint output."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a 'Prior art' note distinguishing this gate from check_shellcheck.py/SC2115: SC2115 already flags standalone `scripts/**/*.sh`, so the new gate's differentiated scope is the test-execs-a-script axis — a shell script (or inline heredoc/script string) reached via subprocess from a pytest test — and it should defer to SC2115 for files SC2115 already scans, avoiding double-reporting.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the gate's detection mechanism and scan scope: state which tree(s)/globs it walks (e.g. shell scripts under tests/ and scripts/, and/or Python tests under tests/**), and — if the test-to-script coupling is in scope — how it resolves the exec'd script from a subprocess call versus analyzing shell scripts directly.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'A gate flags a test that subprocess-execs a shell script containing an unguarded destructive deletion (rm -rf against an interpolated variable).'","AC2/AC3 describe shell-script content: '\"${RM_CMD:-rm}\"' and ': \"${dir:?}\" plus an explicit deny-list' — i.e. the analyzed unit is the script text, not the test.","Summary: 'the specific offending test is not on main (it lives on the unmerged fix-mcp-clone-blocks-boot branch), so this gates the class rather than that one file' — so the offending .sh may not be committed for a direct-scan gate to see.","check_raw_git_writes.py Layer W scans scripts/*.sh directly (SCAN over .sh files), while check_wall_clock_asserts.py scans tests/**.py — the two named precedents scan DIFFERENT trees, so 'consistent with' does not disambiguate which one applies here."],"finding":"The plan does not specify the detection MECHANISM/scope that ties the two coupled artifacts of the incident together: a Python test that subprocess-execs a shell script whose body contains the unguarded rm -rf. AC1 frames it as flagging 'a test that subprocess-execs a shell script,' but the pass/fail fixtures (AC2/AC3) are shell-script CONTENT shapes. It is left ambiguous whether the gate scans .sh files directly for the unguarded shape (like check_raw_git_writes.py Layer W over scripts/*.sh) or must trace a Python test's subprocess call to the script it invokes and analyze that script — and, correspondingly, which tree(s) the gate walks.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe3a88f307d293c9a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC1) vs AC2/AC3; Summary","norm_id":"n2e0e06730d72505e","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A gate that only scans committed scripts/*.sh never sees the incident shape if the offending script lives with the test under tests/ or on an unmerged branch.","A gate that scans Python tests for subprocess calls needs a rule to resolve WHICH script is exec'd and read its body — a step not described, so an implementer could build a shape mismatched to the incident."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Reword AC1 to name the analyzed unit precisely (e.g. 'flags a shell script — including one invoked by a test's subprocess exec — that contains rm -rf against an interpolated variable') and add a scope line stating the file trees/suffixes scanned, mirroring check_raw_git_writes.py's Layer W .sh scan.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: better"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Justify what check_destructive_test_exec.py catches that the existing check_shellcheck.py SC2115 gate (already in `make lint`, already scanning tests/**/*.sh at `-S warning`) does not — or fold the requirement into the existing gate instead of adding a second one.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.785,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["scripts/check_shellcheck.py docstring: 'The motivating defect is **SC2115**:: rm -rf \"${dir}\"/* ... expanded to `rm -rf /*` ... and destroyed `/opt/homebrew` and `/Applications`'","scripts/check_shellcheck.py SEVERITY = 'warning' with comment 'raising this to `error` would silence the very finding this gate exists to catch'","check_shellcheck.discover() uses root.rglob('*.sh') excluding only .venv/.git/.claude/.tickets-*/node_modules — so tests/**/*.sh are already scanned","Makefile:266 `python scripts/check_shellcheck.py` is already wired into `make lint`","sibling ticket e668-b496-e264-4283 declares `relates_to fe4e-54a5-3c3a-4901`, the shellcheck ticket"],"finding":"The proposed gate rebuilds functionality that scripts/check_shellcheck.py already provides: that gate runs in `make lint`, its documented load-bearing purpose is SC2115 (the exact `rm -rf \"${dir}\"/*` unguarded-deletion shape from the same 2026-08-26 incident), its severity floor is deliberately `-S warning` so SC2115 fires, and its discover() already walks tests/**/*.sh. The plan never acknowledges this overlap or states what the new Python-AST gate catches that SC2115 does not.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1833dfa487929345","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC1) / Summary / Notes","norm_id":"n928cbfba5d399a5b","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A test-exec'd shell script contains `rm -rf \"${dir}\"/*` — SC2115 at warning already flags it under the existing gate","The plan's AC3 hardened shape (`: \"${dir:?}\"` + deny-list) is exactly the remediation check_shellcheck.py's own teaching message already recommends (lines 108-111)"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a section to the plan comparing coverage against check_shellcheck.py/SC2115: name the concrete shape(s) the new gate flags that SC2115 misses (e.g. deletion in a Python-invoked script SC2115 cannot statically follow, or a test-file coupling dimension), or drop the standalone gate and extend the shellcheck gate / its exclusion policy.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","seve